      "ogDescription": "Nota de prueba de impresión de la prensa Giori, con los retratos de Lincoln, Washington y Grant, sin denominación. Colección privada Notofilia.",
      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/giori-press-test-note/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <a href=\"/en/collection/us-department-of-the-treasury/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:24px;\">&larr; U.S. Department of the Treasury</a>\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center;\">\n\n        <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:720px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n          <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">Printer's Proof Note &middot; United States &middot; c. 1970</span>\n\n          <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px); line-height:1.08; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">Giori Press Test Note</h1>\n\n          <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">No Denomination &middot; Lincoln, Washington, and Grant</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:560px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 56px;\">\n          <button\n            data-zoom-trigger=\"us-giori-press-test-note\"\n            aria-label=\"Enlarge imagen de la nota de prueba\"\n            style=\"all:unset; display:block; width:100%; position:relative; cursor:zoom-in;\"\n          >\n            <picture>\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/us-giori-press-test-note-640.webp 640w, /uploads/us-giori-press-test-note.webp 1873w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 560px\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img\n                src=\"/uploads/us-giori-press-test-note.jpg\"\n                alt=\"Giori press proof with the portraits of Lincoln, Washington, and Grant cancelled by horizontal lines, obverse above and nearly blank reverse below\"\n                width=\"1873\"\n                height=\"1681\"\n                loading=\"eager\"\n                decoding=\"async\"\n                style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:auto;\"\n              />\n            </picture>\n            <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:22px; right:22px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.82); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; padding:8px 14px; border-radius:999px;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; background:#d8d2cd; transform:rotate(45deg);\"></span>Enlarge</span>\n          </button>\n          <span style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33; text-align:center; font-style:italic;\">Front (top) and almost blank back (bottom) &mdash; Collection of Notophilia.com</span>\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Country</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">United States</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Origin</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Test print commissioned by American Can Company from a plant in Geneva, New York, to calibrate a Giori intaglio press intended for the Bureau of Engraving and Printing</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Denomination</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">None &mdash; is not a legal tender bill, but a technical proof sheet</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Approximate Date</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">1970s</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Type of Issue</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Printer's proof note (<em>press test note</em>), without legal tender or endorsement of any kind</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Catalog Reference</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">No Friedberg or Pick number; cataloged in specialist exonumia literature as a &ldquo;Giori Press Test Note&rdquo;</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n\n          \n            <div\n              role=\"dialog\"\n              aria-modal=\"true\"\n              aria-label=\"Nota ampliada\"\n              data-zoom-dialog=\"us-giori-press-test-note\" hidden\n             \n             class=\"catalog-zoom-dialog\">\n              <button\n                data-zoom-close\n                aria-label=\"Close\"\n                style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; right:28px; background:transparent; border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.4); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:22px; line-height:1; width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:50%; cursor:pointer;\"\n              >&times;</button>\n\n              <div style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; left:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.5); border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.25); border-radius:999px; padding:6px;\">\n                <button type=\"button\" data-zoom-out\n                  disabled=\"true\"\n                  aria-label=\"Zoom out\"\n                  style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\"\n                >&minus;</button>\n                <span data-zoom-percent style=\"min-width:56px; text-align:center; font-size:14px; color:#e7ddc4; letter-spacing:0.05em;\">100%</span>\n                <button\n                  disabled=\"false\"\n                  data-zoom-in aria-label=\"Zoom in\"\n                  style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\"\n                >&#43;</button>\n              </div>\n\n              <div\n                style=\"overflow:hidden; max-width:100vw; max-height:100vh; width:100vw; height:100vh; touch-action:none;\"\n              >\n                <picture>\n                  <source srcset=\"/uploads/us-giori-press-test-note.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n                  <img data-zoom-image\n                    src=\"/uploads/us-giori-press-test-note.jpg\"\n                    alt=\"Nota de prueba de la prensa Giori, enlarged view\"\n                    draggable=\"false\"\n                    style=\"display:block; max-width:100vw; max-height:100vh; width:100vw; height:100vh; object-fit:contain; transform:; cursor:zoom-in; user-select:none;\"\n                  />\n                </picture>\n              </div>\n\n              <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:16px; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:#b7ab8a; font-style:italic; pointer-events:none;\">Drag to move &middot; Mouse wheel to zoom</span>\n            </div>\n          \n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px;\">\n          \n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Historical and Issue Context</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">The Giori Press:</strong>In the mid-twentieth century, the Swiss engineer Gualtiero Giori developed an intaglio printing press capable of printing several colors in a single pass, revolutionizing the production of paper money. The Bureau of Engraving and Printing (BEP) of the United States adopted this technology to modernize the printing of the dollar.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">A subcontracted test note:</strong>This example was produced on behalf of the American Can Company at a test facility in Geneva, New York, for the specific purpose of calibrating and fine-tuning a new Giori press prior to delivery and installation at the BEP. It does not represent real money nor was it ever legal tender.</p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">A collage of existing plates:</strong>Instead of engraving a new design, technicians reused existing plates of one, two, five, and fifty-dollar bills to test the color and printing register of the new press, resulting in a historically unique document that combines elements of several denominations into a single piece with no face value.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Key Details Visible in the Note</h2>\n            <ul style=\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px;\">\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Three engraved portraits:</strong>Abraham Lincoln, George Washington, and Ulysses S. Grant, taken directly from the plates used to print the one-, five-, and fifty-dollar bills.</span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Cancellation lines:</strong>three thick horizontal bands cross each portrait, a deliberate device to prevent the test note from being mistaken for legal tender or used fraudulently.</span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Top legend:</strong>&ldquo;THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA&rdquo; in a typographic arc taken from the back of the five-dollar bill, with solid blocks deliberately superimposed on part of the letters &mdash;, another proof of press registration.</span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Side panels:</strong>vertical ornamental medallions with the word &ldquo;FIVE&rdquo; repeated, taken from the fine decorative engraving of the five-dollar bill.</span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Nearly blank reverse:</strong>Only a faint ghosting or ink transfer from the front is visible, typical of a technical test where the back was not part of the main calibration target.</span>\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Additional Context</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">Outside of any standard numismatic cataloging system (it does not appear in Friedberg or Pick, as it is not legal tender), this type of proof note belongs rather to the realm of industrial exonumia: a technical document from the BEP modernization era that is extremely rare today, prized by collectors specializing in printing proofs and the history of the technology behind the US dollar.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:32px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); padding-top:24px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 12px; font-style:normal;\">Sources</h2>\n            <ul style=\"margin:0; padding:0 0 0 20px; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; color:#5c4e33; font-style:italic;\">\n              <li>Bureau of Engraving and Printing —<a href=\"https://www.bep.gov\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">bep.gov<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>\n              <li>Heritage Auctions —<a href=\"https://www.ha.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">ha.com<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>\n              <li>Numista —<a href=\"https://en.numista.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color:#6b521f;\">numista.com<span style=\"font-style:italic; font-weight:400;\">(opens in a new tab)</span></a></li>\n            </ul>\n          </section>\n\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
      "recordTitle": "Giori Press Test Note",
      "eyebrow": "Nota de Prueba de Imprenta · United States · c. 1970"
